    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7e2b52e8-c533-566d-8a82-a5b33b756b60",
      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-2)=2\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{2}=2-(-2)=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{3}=-2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(4)-(-2)=4\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=4-(-4)-(2)=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=6$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=-2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $\u27e86,4,-2\u27e9.$",
